inline constexpr ManualBlock kManualBlocks_en_2[] = {
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(A native .sxl file stores an editable image document. Paint 3D projects use .sx3d. A flattened export is a delivery image; it does not replace the editable project.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(heading)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Create and open)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(File > New chooses size, precision and Layers or Node mode. Templates provide a configured starting stack or graph. File > New Paint 3D Project starts model painting.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Ctrl+O opens a supported image or document. Ctrl+Shift+O imports an image as a layer. Dropping a file can open a document, import an image or insert a resource according to its type and drop target. Use File > Open for a supplied .sxl example when you want the whole example composition.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(heading)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Save editable work)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Use one native master for continued editing and separate, clearly named exports for delivery. Save As creates a new working path; it is also the base for later relative graph exports. Opening a bundled practice example starts an unsaved copy, so Save asks for a new destination.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Layers mode builds a stack; Node mode gives direct image connections. Converting a layer stack exposes its generated graph. Returning an arbitrary custom graph to Layers is only offered when the structure can be represented; do not assume every graph is reversible to a layer stack. Save a version before changing modes.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Ctrl+S saves; Ctrl+Shift+S chooses another path. A changed document has an unsaved marker. Closing it offers save, discard and cancel.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Save before running export tools with relative filenames: they resolve beside the saved document. An unsaved document uses exports/ beside the executable.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(A linked smart object still depends on its external source. Moving only the parent document does not relocate that source. Embed content for a self-contained handoff.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(heading)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Templates and precision)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(File > Save as Template creates a reusable starting document and metadata. Templates start whole documents; functions insert reusable nodes. User templates are in %LOCALAPPDATA%\Shaderixel\Templates. Shipped templates are in templates/ beside the installed executable.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Use 32-bit float for UV coordinate fields, signed distances and calculations outside 0 to 1. Preview colors may clip while the underlying values remain valid. A high-precision document does not make an 8-bit PNG export high precision.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(link)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Export and delivery)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(export)SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(link)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Smart objects)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(smart_objects)SXMAN"},
};
inline constexpr ManualBlock kManualBlocks_en_3[] = {
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Layers compose from the bottom of the stack upward. Select a layer to edit it in Properties. Visibility hides its contribution; locking prevents editing. Opacity and blending control how it combines with layers below.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(image)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Baking changes the content while keeping mask, opacity and blend editable.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(media/layers_en.png)SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(heading)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Layer types)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(bullet)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Pixel: paintable image content.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(bullet)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Fill / Draw: procedural content without an input image.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(bullet)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Adjustment: an effect applied to the composite below.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(bullet)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Shape: editable geometry, fill and stroke.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(bullet)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Text: editable text and typography.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(bullet)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Smart object: embedded or linked reusable content.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(bullet)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Group: a container for child layers.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Ctrl+Shift+N adds a pixel layer. Ctrl+J duplicates, or creates a layer via copy if a selection exists. Ctrl+G groups; Ctrl+Shift+G ungroups. Reordering changes the composite.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(heading)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Non-destructive filters)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(A layer filter keeps its parameters editable. Disable or remove it to compare with the original. A destructive filter changes the pixel target directly. An adjustment layer processes the result below rather than becoming paintable content.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Styles such as shadows, glows, borders and bevels depend on coverage. Leave canvas space for effects extending beyond the shape.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(heading)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Bake to Pixel Layer)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Use Properties > Bake to Pixel Layer, Layer > Bake to Pixel Layer or the layer context menu. This converts rendered content, its transform and its filters into document-sized editable pixels. It supports generators, text, shapes, smart objects and pixel layers with filters.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(The layer keeps its stack position, name, visibility, mask, opacity, clipping and blending settings. These composition controls remain editable. Source text, shape and filter controls are replaced by pixels. Ctrl+Z restores the original editable layer.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Unlock the target first. Groups and adjustment layers use merge commands instead. Baking one smart-object instance does not edit its source or other instances.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(heading)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(History and snapshots)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Layer compositions record variants of layer state, including visibility, opacity, blending, filter enablement and smart-object placement. They reuse the same layer pixels rather than making independent document copies. Name a composition, adjust the stack and record another, then recall/export the intended state. Painting shared source pixels can affect several variants.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Undo/Redo steps through edits in the current session. Create Snapshot in History captures a complete document state, including layers, parameters, pixels and color profile. Selecting a snapshot restores that state, so preserve the current work before switching to an older snapshot. A snapshot is not an exported image or a substitute for saving the native project.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(heading)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Merge choices)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Ctrl+E merges down. Ctrl+Shift+E merges visible layers. Flatten combines the visible result. Save an editable native copy before discarding the original stack.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(link)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Masks and selections)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(masks)SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(link)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Blending and Blend If)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(blending)SXMAN"},
};
