inline constexpr ManualBlock kManualBlocks_en_42[] = {
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Start with the smallest check that distinguishes the likely causes. Preserve the editable file before destructive experiments. Undo, snapshots, exported images and saved native versions serve different purposes.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(image)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Check view, target, connections and retained results before export)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(media/recovery_en.png)SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(heading)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Empty or unexpected image)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(step)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(1. Select Final Image view, a normal display overlay and the intended material channel.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(step)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(2. Inspect visibility, opacity, blend, Blend If, clipping, masks and the canvas bounds.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(step)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(3. In Node mode, follow the selected output back to a nonempty image. Check multi-output ports and optional inputs.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(step)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(4. Distinguish a .sxfn node resource from a complete .sxl example. A pixel surface in a pixel-free function starts empty.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(step)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(5. A tool can show its live input before execution. Run its event to obtain a retained result, then rerun after upstream edits or clear stored results to return to live data.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(heading)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Nothing paints or transforms)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Check the unlocked target and its image/mask thumbnail, selection, foreground color, brush opacity/flow and current view. Convert procedural content to pixels or paint on a new pixel layer. A shape's geometry dimensions, a layer's transformed bounds and canvas dimensions are separate. Decimal pixel fields can be entered manually; image dimensions eventually require integral raster sizes.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(If pressure is constant, check the tablet backend and driver, then test a brush that actually uses pressure. A mouse does not supply every pen channel. If a numeric control seems inert, it may be disabled by Auto, an active link or the current document mode.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(heading)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Shader compilation or missing resources)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Open Edit > Shader Errors and inspect shaderixel.log. Check the failing stable shader ID, parameter types, source syntax and image input count. Reloading a renamed file does not repair references to its previous ID. A function that works on another machine may depend on a user library effect or external texture.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(For tile seams, check neighbor support, UV sampling and halo metadata. For dark alpha edges, check premultiplication conventions. For strange UV/SDF values, use float precision and avoid color-transfer conversions or unintended clamping. Compile errors must be fixed before comparing a preview to final output.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(heading)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Memory and slow work)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Pixel storage grows with width × height × channels × bytes per component, multiplied by layers, masks, intermediates and retained results. Doubling each dimension uses roughly four times as many pixels. GPU history also competes for VRAM.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Reduce preview size, expensive blur/sampling radii, brush size/dab density, render samples or simulation resolution while tuning. Keep the final quality requirements for export. Large-image tiled rendering limits some working allocations but does not make every arbitrary full-image shader cheap. Use History memory Auto or sensible budgets; lowering them can forget older edits.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Clear obsolete retained results if live recomputation is wanted. Full-resolution AI/upscale sources may be larger than the graph preview. CPU rendering is an alternative for presentation rendering, not a switch that runs every image shader on the CPU.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(heading)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(File and environment recovery)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(bullet)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Save a new native version before repacking UVs, merging, flattening or resetting a complex setup.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(bullet)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(If closing/updating prompts about unsaved work, Cancel keeps it open; do not assume a project has been saved merely because an export completed.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(bullet)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(A missing linked asset needs its source restored/relinked or embedded. A layout reset cannot restore missing pixels.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(bullet)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Close the app before renaming backed-up settings/layout files. Preserve user libraries and project files separately.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(bullet)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(A failed AI request may leave the original live image visible; check endpoint, installed model, API workflow and status rather than exporting that preview as a completed result.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(heading)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(A useful bug report)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(text)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Record app version, GPU/backend/driver, document dimensions/precision, exact steps, expected/actual result and relevant log lines. Reduce a copy to the smallest failing graph or layer stack. Include required user effects/functions or a procedural example where possible. Remove credentials and unrelated private files. A screenshot alone may hide the selected output or target, so describe those explicitly.)SXMAN", R"SXMAN()SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(link)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Settings and update states)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(settings)SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(link)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Shader authoring)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(shader_authoring)SXMAN"},
    {R"SXMAN(link)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(Troubleshooting index)SXMAN", R"SXMAN(troubleshooting)SXMAN"},
};
